oning and heating equipment in the United States and Canada. The company operates through three segments: AAON Oklahoma, AAON Coil Products, and BASX. It offers rooftop units, data center cooling solutions, cleanroom systems, packaged outdoor mechanical rooms, air handling units, makeup air units, energy recovery units, condensing units, geothermal/water-source heat pumps, coils, and controls. The company markets and sells its products to retail, manufacturing, educational, lodging, supermarket, data centers, medical and pharmaceutical, and other commercial industries. It sells its products through a network of independent manufacturer representative organizations and internal sales force, as well as online. AAON, Inc. was incorporated in 1987 and is headquartered in Tulsa, Oklahoma.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Matthew J. Tobolski Ph.D., SE | President, CEO & Director | Age 41 | Compensation: $975,345 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $245K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["AAON, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $6.6B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years and +15% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 10-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 28%.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 8.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.5%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 17% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 423% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":4.231409225592745},{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +6.3% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (80% sell ratio, net $10.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","20 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Makes Aaon (AAON) a New Strong Buy Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029739/what-makes-aaon-aaon-a-new-strong-buy-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_12_zacks_rank_upgrade-3029739","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794585603.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why AAON Stock Surged 37.8% This Week","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/why-aaon-stock-surged-37-145352000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794581961.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Wall Street Analysts Think Aaon (AAON) Could Surge 34.26%: Read This Before Placing a Bet","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029554/wall-street-analysts-think-aaon-aaon-could-surge-34-26-read-this-before-placing-a-bet?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cconsensus_price_target-3029554","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794578103.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Critical Analysis: AAON (NASDAQ:AAON) & Armstrong World Industries (NYSE:AWI)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/critical-analysis-aaon-nasdaqaaon-armstrong-world-industries-nyseawi.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794572328.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.876,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"AAON, Inc. Just Beat Analyst Forecasts, And Analysts Have Been Updating Their Predictions","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-aaon/aaon/news/aaon-inc-just-beat-analyst-forecasts-and-analysts-have-been","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794485763.406,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.556,"